**Short Story:**  
Kip the Gnome Warlock scratched his head as his Succubus, Vex, lounged on a nearby rock in Stranglethorn Vale, watching him fiddle with a broken fishing rod. “You’re supposed to help,” he muttered. Vex yawned, then lazily flicked her tail—*poof*—and the rod fixed itself. Kip grinned. Later, when a bandit gang ambushed them, Vex didn’t just fight—she whispered to them, and two dropped their weapons mid-swing. “You’re a sneaky little thing,” Kip laughed, as they walked away with loot.  

**Answer:**  
Succubus has *Seduction*, which makes it easier to avoid unnecessary fights, bypass enemies, and gather info—this makes it more versatile for questing than Voidwalker, even if Voidwalker is tankier. Warlocks favor Voidwalkers for aesthetics, but Succubus is more common *in practice* because of this skill. [end of text]


